Administrator Hierarchy: System & Municipal Administrators,TPS-ADD-1,"h2. Objective

Split the single ""administrator"" role into two operating levels so a platform-wide System Administrator and a city-scoped Municipal Administrator can both manage complaints without a new database role.

----

h2. Description

As a System Administrator,
I want to create, view, and disable Municipal Administrator accounts and see complaints/reports across every city,
So that I can delegate day-to-day complaint handling to city-level staff while retaining global oversight.

As a Municipal Administrator,
I want to be scoped to exactly one city for complaints, field workers, and reports,
So that I only see and act on the data relevant to my own municipality.

Implemented via a new administrator_profiles table (admin_level: system|municipal, city_id, created_by_id) composed onto the existing User model — no 4th role was added. Backed by require_admin_level/require_system_admin/require_municipal_admin RBAC decorators.

----

h2. Deliverables

* administrator_profiles table + migration
* GET/POST /admin/municipal-administrators, GET/PUT/DELETE /admin/municipal-administrators/{id}
* City-scoping enforced on /admin/complaints, /admin/field-workers, /reports/*
* Municipal Administrators page (system-admin-only) in the frontend

----

h2. Acceptance Criteria

# System Administrator can register a Municipal Administrator with exactly one city.
# Municipal Administrators cannot self-register.
# Municipal Administrators only see/act on complaints, field workers, and reports for their own city.
# System Administrators remain unscoped across all cities.
# No new row is added to the roles table; both levels share the administrator role."
City & Pincode Master Data + Public Locations API,TPS-ADD-2,"h2. Objective

Give citizens a pincode-first location experience instead of a free-text address field, and give administrators a city master table to scope onboarding and reporting against.

----

h2. Description

As a Citizen,
I want to type my 6-digit pincode and have the city auto-resolve (or be prompted to choose when a pincode maps to more than one city),
So that I do not have to manually type my city name and city data stays consistent platform-wide.

As a System Administrator,
I want a cities master table populated from a CSV import,
So that Municipal Administrator onboarding and complaint routing use consistent city records instead of free text.

----

h2. Deliverables

* cities and city_pincodes tables + migrations
* flask import-pincodes CLI command (loads database/pincode.csv, --replace to rebuild)
* Public /api/v1/locations namespace (no JWT required): pincode lookup, city autosuggest, pincode autocomplete, reverse-geocode, landing-page overview stats, public complaint map pins

----

h2. Acceptance Criteria

# GET /locations/pincode/{pincode} returns match_count so the UI can block/auto-select/prompt.
# GET /locations/cities and /locations/pincodes support autosuggest/autocomplete.
# flask import-pincodes is idempotent by default and supports a --replace flag to rebuild.
# All /locations/* endpoints are public (no authentication required)."
Mandatory Photo-First Pothole Reporting with Map Pin,TPS-ADD-3,"h2. Objective

Narrow the product scope to pothole-only reporting and require a photo plus a map pin at submission time, instead of an optional photo and free-text address.

----

h2. Description

As a Citizen,
I want to be required to attach a photo and drop a map pin when reporting a pothole,
So that administrators and field workers receive verifiable, precisely-located reports instead of ambiguous text descriptions.

----

h2. Deliverables

* Mandatory image_url on complaint submission (upload-then-reference pattern, instance/uploads/complaints/)
* Map pin capture (latitude/longitude) surfaced on the citizen report form and on admin/field-worker complaint detail views
* Public complaint-pins endpoint for the landing-page map

----

h2. Acceptance Criteria

# A complaint cannot be submitted without a photo.
# A complaint cannot be submitted without a map pin (latitude/longitude).
# The uploaded photo is retrievable by URL from the citizen, admin, and field-worker views.
# The public landing page displays a map of reported complaint locations."
Administrator-Driven Password Reset & Email Update,TPS-ADD-4,"h2. Objective

Give System and Municipal Administrators a way to reset a forgotten password or correct an email address for the accounts they manage, without requiring SMTP/email infrastructure.

----

h2. Description

As a System Administrator,
I want to reset a Municipal Administrator's or a Citizen's password and correct their email address,
So that a locked-out user can regain access without needing a self-service email flow that the platform does not yet support.

As a Municipal Administrator,
I want to reset a Field Worker's (or my own city's Citizens') password and correct their email address,
So that I can support my team directly.

----

h2. Deliverables

* Optional email/password/confirm_password fields added to PUT /admin/users/{id}, PUT /admin/field-workers/{id}, PUT /admin/municipal-administrators/{id}
* /admin/users (list/get/put) opened to Municipal Administrators, scoped server-side to citizens in their own city
* Separate ""Edit Details"" and ""Reset Password"" actions in the frontend (Citizens.vue, MunicipalAdministrators.vue, FieldWorkers.vue)

----

h2. Acceptance Criteria

# A System Administrator can reset any user's password and it takes effect on next login.
# A System Administrator can change a Municipal Administrator's or Citizen's email (unique, conflict returns 409).
# A Municipal Administrator can reset a Field Worker's password and change their email, scoped to their own city.
# A Municipal Administrator can view, edit, and reset the password of Citizens in their own city only (404 outside their city).
# ""Edit Details"" and ""Reset Password"" are two separate actions/buttons in the UI, not one combined form."
